+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a length of time to a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. The value is either a whole
+number of seconds, like `120`, or one or more `<integer><unit>` groups with the units `d`, `h`, `m`, and `s`, like
+`2d`, `1h30m`, or `1d2h3m4s`. Each unit may be used at most once, in that order, without spaces. Units are
+case-insensitive.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s", show_default=True)
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting {timeout.total_seconds():g} seconds.")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--help'])
+```
+
